From 88024787ef9cde91dbf3dcd27e54c908a5e72a46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joris-sta <joris-sta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:45:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gdn: chunk-staged gated delta net kernel for pre-tensor-core
 GPUs

Recurrent hybrid models execute their gated-delta-net memory layer on a
new sm_61 kernel (gdn-chunk-pascal.cuh, GGML_CUDA_GDN_PASCAL=
auto|off|staged, GGML_CUDA_GDN_PASCAL_CHUNK=16|32). Each warp holds a
permanent register shard of the D*D recurrent state; per-CTA token tiles
stream B tokens at a time and reuse normalized Q/K across C value
columns, amortizing global loads while preserving the exact
recurrent/snapshot update order of the reference path.

The fused delta-rule update s = g*s + k*beta*(v - g*(s.k)), output
projection and on-the-fly L2 normalization (sum-of-squares eps or
vectorized L2 modes) run inside the same register loop, with optional
last-K-slot snapshot capture for server state retention.

The Qwen3.5 MTP drafter graph applies the shared Bonsai Hadamard
embedding inverse on nextn token lookup, so draft and target share the
same latent basis (build_get_rows_embd).

test-gdn-chunk-pascal plus extended test-backend-ops coverage hits
chunk-crossing token counts (15..65), multiple sequences, norm
amplitudes across regimes, suffix snapshots and state-cache fusion.
